# Defect 2242, 2026-10-28 (panel 231: the ffi-pragmatist writing a generated
# group's Heroes wrapper by hand, reproduced by the sitting's critic).
# Symptom: a wrapper `done(a: G5)` returning `g5_close(a)`, where `g5_close`
# takes its handle `consumes`, is refused `consumed_borrowed_handle` with its
# caret under the `a` of `g5_close(a)`, and the note said *Mark the parameter
# `@a` and the call site `@a` too*: written at the call the caret is under,
# `g5_close(@a)` is `marker_mismatch`, since a group's consuming parameter
# takes no `@`. Cause: the call site meant was the wrapper's caller's,
# `done(@a)`, spec § 9's pair, and the note named neither the wrapper nor its
# calls. Now it names the function the parameter belongs to, puts the `@` on
# its signature and before the argument at every call of it, and says this
# call stays as it is. `done_well`, the wrapper written as the note says, is
# left alone; the issue's program written so, its `a` a cell as the next
# message asks, checks clean and built prints `0` (this Mac, 2026-10-29).
extern "fixedbugs-2242-a-wrapper-ending-its-borrowed-handle-is-told-where-the-at-goes.h"
    record G5 tag g5_acc
    function g5_open(start: i64) -> G5 acquires g5_close
    function g5_close(a: G5 consumes) -> i32

# The issue's own wrapper.
function done(a: G5) -> i32
    return g5_close(a)  #~ consumed_borrowed_handle

# Left alone: the wrapper the note writes, called with `@` on a cell.
function done_well(@a: G5) -> i32
    return g5_close(a)

function main()
    a = g5_open(start: 1)
    print(done(a))
    b: G5 @= g5_open(start: 2)
    print(done_well(@b))
